Description: HF / shortwave SDR receiver for the SDRplay RSP1
 RSPSDR turns an SDRplay RSP1 into a shortwave and amateur-band receiver:
 a live spectrum and rolling waterfall, tuning by click or dial, and the
 usual HF demodulators.
 .
 Features:
  * Spectrum and waterfall with auto-tracking levels, nine colour maps,
    1x-16x zoom and an adjustable waterfall resolution.
  * AM, synchronous AM, USB, LSB, CW with adjustable pitch, and NFM, each
    with its passband drawn on the spectrum where the demodulator really
    puts it.
  * Audio AGC, squelch, and spectral-subtraction noise reduction that
    measurably improves the signal-to-noise ratio on a noisy carrier and
    leaves a clean one untouched.
  * Memory channels, band and preset jumping, and RF/IF gain controls.
  * Headless modes: --check, --selftest, --wav, --memories.
 .
 The SDRplay module and the SDRplay API are not part of Debian, so they are
 recommended rather than required and this package installs on a plain
 Debian system.
